  "result": "Subcommands now pick up their defaults from `default_map`. I fixed it in `src/click/core.py` (`Context.__init__`, around line 392).\n\nA child context was inheriting the parent's whole `default_map`. A subcommand's options were therefore looked up in the top-level map instead of under the subcommand's own entry. It now takes `parent.default_map.get(info_name)`.\n\nI checked it with a group that has a `sub` command with `--x`, run with `default_map={\"sub\": {\"x\": \"mapped\"}}`. The output is `mapped`. The full suite passes (1906 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed).\n\nSubcommands with no entry in the map now get no default from it, instead of falling back to the parent's map.\n\nI haven't added a regression test for this, or for the earlier fixes and `KeyValue`. I can add them if you want.",
